  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-02-04T20:26:00.160Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Just as an example, It's near impossible to keep any form of order in a courtroom when people with attention disorders keep messing about, trolling with the buttons, props and other people. Votekicking is very buggy and doesn't work half the time - it would be great if we could create public instances where we/room creators can kick people from the room right away just like in a private instance. However, the difference is that this is a public room, and people can continue to join without invites. A big problem with private instance courtrooms, aside from the obvious is that we can't continue to recruit new people when somebody has to leave. Shifting worlds and reinviting people a million times is very time consuming and harder than it needs to be. So it would save a lot of headaches if we could create a public instance where the room creators can kick people freely. Of course, this should be a different kind of instance (different from default) and the people joining should be aware that the room creator has the ability to kick them before joining (to control griefing).",
